IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa18-part24.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 24 (annual confirmation of accuracy of information on
-- register), ss 853A to 859. Lines 11426-11596 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- How to read an answer (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING) is as in the header of coa18-part22-notice.l4.
--
-- PERIODS. s 827 (working days) is in Part 22 and applies to "any provision of this Part" (Part 22) only: the 14 days of s 853A(1)
-- and s 853L(1) are counted in calendar days, the day after the end of the review period being the first. The period of 14
-- days "after the end of each review period" ends on the fourteenth day after the last day of the review period, and a
-- statement delivered on that day is in time (fork register).
-- 12 MONTHS. "the period of 12 months beginning with the day of the company's incorporation" ends on the day before the first
-- anniversary of that day, an incorporation on 29 February having its anniversary on 1 March of a year that is not a leap year
-- (fork register).
-- SEAMS (inputs): `s 9(5)(c) ...`, `s 86(2) ...`, `s 87 ...`, `s 88A(2) ...`, `s 88B ...`, `s 790B ...` (Part 21A does not apply),
-- `s 167I`, `s 279I`, `s 790LG`, `s 167G`/`s 167H`, `s 279G`/`s 279H`, `s 790LA` to `s 790LH` (the duties s 853B lists),
-- `s 1121 the officer is in default`, `s 251 the person is a shadow director`, `s 1167` (prescribed).
-- ANSWERS OTHER PARTS ASK FOR (PLAN section 6): `s 853A(3)` confirmation period and confirmation date, `s 853A(1)` confirmation
-- statement, `s 853A(5)` and `s 853A(6)` review period, `s 853E(6)` DTR5 issuer and relevant market.

§ `Part 24 (ss 853A to 859): annual confirmation of accuracy of information on register`

§§ `s 853A Duty to deliver confirmation statements`

-- (5): a review period is 12 months beginning with a day. The first begins with the day of incorporation; each later one begins
-- with the day after the end of the previous one. The function gives the last day of the review period that begins on a day.
-- src:11439 | (5) For the purposes of this Part, each of the following is a review period—
-- src:11440 | (a) the period of 12 months beginning with the day of the company's incorporation;
-- src:11441 | (b) each period of 12 months beginning with the day after the end of the previous review period.
@ref s 853A(5) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11439-11441)
GIVEN `the first day of the review period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 853A(5) the last day of the review period beginning on the day` MEANS
    Date (Day (Date (DATE_DAY `the first day of the review period`) (DATE_MONTH `the first day of the review period`) (DATE_YEAR `the first day of the review period` PLUS 1)) MINUS 1)

-- (6): where a confirmation statement is delivered with a confirmation date earlier than the last day of the review period
-- concerned, the next review period begins the day after the confirmation date; otherwise the day after the last day.
-- src:11442 | (6) But where a company delivers a confirmation statement with a confirmation date which is earlier than the last day of the review period concerned, the next review period is the period of 12 months beginning with the day after the confirmation date.
@ref s 853A(6) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11442-11442)
GIVEN `the last day of the review period concerned` IS A DATE
      `the confirmation date of the statement delivered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 853A(6) the first day of the next review period` MEANS
    IF Day `the confirmation date of the statement delivered` LESS THAN Day `the last day of the review period concerned`
    THEN Date (Day `the confirmation date of the statement delivered` PLUS 1)
    ELSE Date (Day `the last day of the review period concerned` PLUS 1)

-- src:11438 | (4) The confirmation date of a confirmation statement must be no later than the last day of the review period concerned.
@ref s 853A(4) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11438-11438)
GIVEN `the confirmation date of the statement` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the review period concerned` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853A(4) the confirmation date is no later than the last day of the review period concerned` MEANS
    IF Day `the confirmation date of the statement` AT MOST Day `the last day of the review period concerned`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The confirmation date of a confirmation statement must be no later than the last day of the review period concerned."

-- (3): the confirmation period begins with the day of incorporation (the first statement) or the day after the confirmation date
-- of the last such statement (any other), and ends with the confirmation date of the statement concerned.
-- src:11435 | (3) In this Part “confirmation period”—
-- src:11436 | (a) in relation to a company's first confirmation statement, means the period beginning with the day of the company's incorporation and ending with the date specified in the statement (“the confirmation date”);
-- src:11437 | (b) in relation to any other confirmation statement of a company, means the period beginning with the day after the confirmation date of the last such statement and ending with the confirmation date of the confirmation statement concerned.
@ref s 853A(3) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11435-11437)
GIVEN `the statement is the company's first confirmation statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the company's incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the confirmation date of the last such statement` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 853A(3) the first day of the confirmation period` MEANS
    IF `the statement is the company's first confirmation statement`
    THEN JUST `the day of the company's incorporation`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the confirmation date of the last such statement`
         WHEN JUST lastDate THEN JUST (Date (Day lastDate PLUS 1))
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a later statement needs the confirmation date of the last statement, which is not given

@ref s 853A(3) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11435-11437)
GIVEN `the date specified in the statement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 853A(3) the confirmation date and the last day of the confirmation period` MEANS
    `the date specified in the statement`

-- (1): the duty and its time limit. The 14 days are counted in calendar days from the day after the last day of the review period.
-- src:11428 | (1) Every company must, before the end of the period of 14 days after the end of each review period, deliver to the registrar—
-- src:11429 | (a) such information as is necessary to ensure that the company is able to make the statement referred to in paragraph (b), and
-- src:11430 | (b) a statement (a “confirmation statement”) confirming—
-- src:11431 | (i) that the company has delivered to the registrar, or is delivering to the registrar at the same time as the confirmation statement, all of the information that it is required to deliver in relation to the confirmation period concerned under any duty to notify a relevant event (see section 853B),
-- src:11432 | (ii) that the company is delivering to the registrar at the same time as the confirmation statement any information that it is required to deliver by virtue of a duty imposed by any of sections 853BA to 853H, and
-- src:11433 | (iii) in the case of a company’s first statement under this paragraph, that the company has delivered to the registrar, or is delivering to the registrar at the same time as the confirmation statement, any information that it is required to deliver under section 167I, 279I or 790LG (pre-incorporation changes).
@ref s 853A(1) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11428-11433)
GIVEN `the last day of the review period` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the confirmation statement was delivered to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853A(1) the confirmation statement was delivered before the end of the period of 14 days after the end of the review period` MEANS
    IF Day `the date on which the confirmation statement was delivered to the registrar` AT MOST (Day `the last day of the review period` PLUS 14)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must, before the end of the period of 14 days after the end of each review period, deliver to the registrar ... a statement (a “confirmation statement”)"

@ref s 853A(1) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11428-11433)
GIVEN `the last day of the review period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 853A(1) the last day of the period of 14 days after the end of the review period` MEANS
    Date (Day `the last day of the review period` PLUS 14)

@ref s 853A(1) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11428-11433)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed after the end of the review period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 853A(1) the company must deliver a confirmation statement to the registrar after the end of each review period` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "s 853A(1) delivers the confirmation statement and the information to the registrar")
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed after the end of the review period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 853A(1): the confirmation statement was not delivered before the end of the period of 14 days after the end of the review period"

@ref s 853A(1) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11429-11429)
GIVEN `the company delivered such information as is necessary to ensure that the company is able to make the statement referred to in paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853A(1)(a) the company delivered the information necessary to make the confirmation statement` MEANS
    IF `the company delivered such information as is necessary to ensure that the company is able to make the statement referred to in paragraph (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must ... deliver to the registrar— (a) such information as is necessary to ensure that the company is able to make the statement referred to in paragraph (b)"

@ref s 853A(1)(b) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11430-11433)
GIVEN `the statement confirms that the company has delivered to the registrar, or is delivering at the same time, all of the information that it is required to deliver in relation to the confirmation period concerned under any duty to notify a relevant event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement confirms that the company is delivering at the same time any information that it is required to deliver by virtue of a duty imposed by any of sections 853BA to 853H` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is the company's first statement under paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement confirms that the company has delivered, or is delivering at the same time, any information that it is required to deliver under section 167I, 279I or 790LG` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853A(1)(b) the confirmation statement confirms what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF     `the statement confirms that the company has delivered to the registrar, or is delivering at the same time, all of the information that it is required to deliver in relation to the confirmation period concerned under any duty to notify a relevant event`
       AND `the statement confirms that the company is delivering at the same time any information that it is required to deliver by virtue of a duty imposed by any of sections 853BA to 853H`
       AND (   (NOT `the statement is the company's first statement under paragraph (b)`)
            OR `the statement confirms that the company has delivered, or is delivering at the same time, any information that it is required to deliver under section 167I, 279I or 790LG`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement (a “confirmation statement”) confirming— (i) that the company has delivered ... all of the information ..., (ii) that the company is delivering ... any information ..., and (iii) in the case of a company’s first statement under this paragraph, that the company has delivered ... any information that it is required to deliver under section 167I, 279I or 790LG (pre-incorporation changes)"

-- src:11443 | (7) For the purpose of making a confirmation statement a company is entitled to assume that information that has been delivered to the registrar has been properly delivered unless the registrar has notified the company otherwise.
@ref s 853A(7) Duty to deliver confirmation statements (src:11443-11443)
GIVEN `the registrar has notified the company that information delivered to the registrar was not properly delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853A(7) the company is entitled to assume that information that has been delivered to the registrar has been properly delivered` MEANS
    IF `the registrar has notified the company that information delivered to the registrar was not properly delivered`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is entitled to assume that information that has been delivered to the registrar has been properly delivered unless the registrar has notified the company otherwise"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 853B Duties to notify a relevant event`

DECLARE `s 853B duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 853B(c) the duty to give notice of a change as mentioned in section 167G or 167H`
    `s 853B(e) the duty to give notice of a change as mentioned in section 279G or 279H`
    `s 853B(g) the duty to deliver anything as mentioned in section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH`
    `s 853B(h) any duty under regulations under section 1136 to give notice of a change in the address of the place where company records are kept`
    `s 853B another duty`

-- src:11444 | 853B Duties to notify a relevant event
-- src:11445 | The following duties are duties to notify a relevant event—
-- src:11446 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11447 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11448 | (c) the duty to give notice of a change as mentioned in section 167G or 167H (changes in directors or required information about a director);
-- src:11449 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11450 | (e) the duty to give notice of a change as mentioned in section 279G or 279H (change in secretary or joint secretaries or in required information about a secretary or joint secretary);
-- src:11451 | (f) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11452 | (fa) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:11453 | (g) the duty to deliver anything as mentioned in section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH (information about persons with significant control);
-- src:11454 | (h) in the case of a company which, in accordance with regulations under section 1136, keeps any company records at a place other than its registered office, any duty under the regulations to give notice of a change in the address of that place.
@ref s 853B Duties to notify a relevant event (src:11444-11454)
GIVEN duty IS A `s 853B duty`
      `the company, in accordance with regulations under section 1136, keeps company records at a place other than its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853B the duty is a duty to notify a relevant event` MEANS
    CONSIDER duty
    WHEN `s 853B(c) the duty to give notice of a change as mentioned in section 167G or 167H` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 853B(e) the duty to give notice of a change as mentioned in section 279G or 279H` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 853B(g) the duty to deliver anything as mentioned in section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 853B(h) any duty under regulations under section 1136 to give notice of a change in the address of the place where company records are kept` THEN
        IF `the company, in accordance with regulations under section 1136, keeps company records at a place other than its registered office`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(h) in the case of a company which, in accordance with regulations under section 1136, keeps any company records at a place other than its registered office"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following duties are duties to notify a relevant event" does not say "only" (paragraphs (a), (b), (d), (f) and (fa) are shown as dots in the text)

§§ `s 853BA Duty to confirm lawful purpose`

-- src:11455 | 853BA Duty to confirm lawful purpose
-- src:11456 | Where a company makes a confirmation statement it must at the same time deliver to the registrar a statement that the intended future activities of the company are lawful.
@ref s 853BA Duty to confirm lawful purpose (src:11455-11456)
GIVEN `the company makes a confirmation statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853BA the company must deliver at the same time a statement that the intended future activities of the company are lawful` MEANS
    IF `the company makes a confirmation statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company makes a confirmation statement it must at the same time deliver to the registrar a statement that the intended future activities of the company are lawful."

@ref s 853BA Duty to confirm lawful purpose (src:11455-11456)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 853BA the company must deliver a statement that its intended future activities are lawful` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "s 853BA delivers, at the same time as the confirmation statement, a statement that the intended future activities of the company are lawful")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 853BA: no statement that the intended future activities are lawful was delivered with the confirmation statement"

§§ `s 853C Duty to notify a change in company's principal business activities`

-- src:11458 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:11459 | (a) a company makes a confirmation statement, and
-- src:11460 | (b) there has been a change in the company's principal business activities during the confirmation period concerned.
@ref s 853C(1) Duty to notify a change in company's principal business activities (src:11458-11460)
GIVEN `the company makes a confirmation statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a change in the company's principal business activities during the confirmation period concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853C(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company makes a confirmation statement` AND `there has been a change in the company's principal business activities during the confirmation period concerned`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) a company makes a confirmation statement, and (b) there has been a change in the company's principal business activities during the confirmation period concerned."

-- src:11461 | (1A) This section also applies where—
-- src:11462 | (a) a company makes its first confirmation statement, and
-- src:11463 | (b) by the time of its incorporation, the company’s principal business activities had changed from those specified in the statement under section 9(5)(c).
@ref s 853C(1A) Duty to notify a change in company's principal business activities (src:11461-11463)
GIVEN `the company makes its first confirmation statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 9(5)(c) by the time of its incorporation the company's principal business activities had changed from those specified in the statement under section 9(5)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853C(1A) this section also applies` MEANS
    IF `the company makes its first confirmation statement` AND `s 9(5)(c) by the time of its incorporation the company's principal business activities had changed from those specified in the statement under section 9(5)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section also applies where— (a) a company makes its first confirmation statement, and (b) by the time of its incorporation, the company’s principal business activities had changed from those specified in the statement under section 9(5)(c)."

-- src:11464 | (2) The company must give notice to the registrar of the change at the same time as it delivers the confirmation statement.
@ref s 853C(2) Duty to notify a change in company's principal business activities (src:11464-11464)
GIVEN `s 853C(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 853C(1A) this section also applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853C(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change at the same time as it delivers the confirmation statement` MEANS
    IF `s 853C(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 853C(1A) this section also applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 853C(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 853C(1A) this section also applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(1) This section applies where ..." and "(1A) This section also applies where ..."
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known

@ref s 853C(2) Duty to notify a change in company's principal business activities (src:11464-11464)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 853C(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change in its principal business activities` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "s 853C(2) gives notice of the change in the company's principal business activities at the same time as the confirmation statement")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 853C(2): notice of the change in principal business activities was not given with the confirmation statement"

-- src:11465 | (3) The information as to the company's new principal business activities may be given by reference to one or more categories of any prescribed system of classifying business activities.
@ref s 853C(3) Duty to notify a change in company's principal business activities (src:11465-11465)
GIVEN `s 1167 the system of classifying business activities is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853C(3) the information may be given by reference to one or more categories of the system` MEANS
    IF `s 1167 the system of classifying business activities is prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be given by reference to one or more categories of any prescribed system of classifying business activities": a system that is not prescribed is not mentioned

§§ `s 853CA Duty to notify a change in registered office`

-- src:11467 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:11468 | (a) a company makes a confirmation statement,
-- src:11469 | (b) the company’s registered office is not at an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2), and
-- src:11470 | (c) the company has not given a notice under section 87 (change of registered office) that is awaiting registration by the registrar.
@ref s 853CA(1) Duty to notify a change in registered office (src:11467-11470)
GIVEN `the company makes a confirmation statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 86(2) the company's registered office is at an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 87 the company has given a notice under section 87 (change of registered office) that is awaiting registration by the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853CA(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF     `the company makes a confirmation statement`
       AND (NOT `s 86(2) the company's registered office is at an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2)`)
       AND (NOT `s 87 the company has given a notice under section 87 (change of registered office) that is awaiting registration by the registrar`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) a company makes a confirmation statement, (b) the company’s registered office is not at an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2), and (c) the company has not given a notice under section 87 ... that is awaiting registration by the registrar."

-- src:11471 | (2) The company must deliver a notice under section 87 at the same time as it delivers the confirmation statement.
@ref s 853CA(2) Duty to notify a change in registered office (src:11471-11471)
GIVEN `s 853CA(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853CA(2) the company must deliver a notice under section 87 at the same time as it delivers the confirmation statement` MEANS
    `s 853CA(1) this section applies` -- JUST TRUE is the duty; JUST FALSE is subsection (1)'s own "where"; NOTHING stays NOTHING

@ref s 853CA(2) Duty to notify a change in registered office (src:11471-11471)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 853CA(2) the company must deliver a notice under section 87 with the confirmation statement` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "s 853CA(2) delivers a notice under section 87 at the same time as the confirmation statement")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 853CA(2): no notice under section 87 was delivered with the confirmation statement"

§§ `s 853CB Duty to notify a change in registered email address`

-- src:11473 | (1) This section applies where—
