§§ `s 853D Duty to deliver statement of capital`

-- src:11479 | (1) This section applies where a company having a share capital makes a confirmation statement.
@ref s 853D(1) Duty to deliver statement of capital (src:11479-11479)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company makes a confirmation statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853D(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company has a share capital` AND `the company makes a confirmation statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company having a share capital makes a confirmation statement."

-- src:11480 | (2) The company must deliver a statement of capital to the registrar at the same time as it delivers the confirmation statement.
