-- src:11570 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (1) is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:11571 | (a) in England and Wales to a fine, and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding the greater of £500 and one-tenth of level 4 on the standard scale;
-- src:11572 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 853L(2) Failure to deliver confirmation statement (src:11570-11572)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 853L(2) penalty`
`s 853L(2) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    --   how convicted,        fine not exceeding,                                           daily default fine for continued contravention (the greater of 500 pounds and one-tenth of level 4 in England and Wales; one-tenth of level 5 elsewhere)
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (`s 853L(2) penalty` OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, JUST (`s 853L(2)(a) the greater of an amount in pounds and a fraction of a level on the standard scale` 500 4 0.1))
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (`s 853L(2) penalty` OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1), JUST (`s 853L(2)(b) a fraction of a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1))
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (`s 853L(2) penalty` OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1), JUST (`s 853L(2)(b) a fraction of a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1))
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on summary conviction— (a) in England and Wales ... (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland": summary conviction is divided by place; a conviction on indictment is not mentioned

